    "summary": "High‑energy late set with Hard To Handle, Not Fade Away & stellar drumming",
    "blurb": "The show bursts into gear with a punchy Hard To Handle and a soaring Not Fade Away that leads into an extended drum odyssey. Jerry’s tone stays fluid throughout while Phil pushes his bass front‑and‑center on the early numbers. The late set keeps momentum with standout takes of Uncle John’s Band, High Time and Caution.",
    "review": "February 14, 1970 at the Fillmore East captured one of the Dead’s most electrifying late‑show performances. From the opening acoustic set into a blistering electric second half, the band rides a wave of tight interplay – Jerry Garcia’s fluid lead work and perfect tone shine on Hard To Handle and the soaring Not Fade Away, while Phil Lesh’s bass is “next level,” especially during that 12‑minute drum segment that, though long‑winded, fuels an epic jam into Mason’s Children, Caution (Do Not Stop On Tracks) and Feedback. The rhythm section—Bill Kreutzmann and Mickey Hart—is repeatedly praised as “on point” and “explosive,” delivering the kind of percussive power that makes this show a fan favorite. Highlights like Uncle John’s Band, High Time, Dark Hollow, Black Peter and Katie Mae add depth to an already rich setlist, making this recording a must‑listen for anyone chasing the early ’70 Dead sound.",
